This photo is from the Mirror Pond Viewpoint on the Bull River Road, Hwy 54, with Ibex and Snowshoe peaks in the background only 2 hours and 15 minutes of easy highway driving from my house in the East Spokane Valley. I love this place. It is a mini Glacier National Park with out all the people. On the other side of the ridge is Granite Lake with a 4,000 foot head wall up to A Peak with several water falls coming off of it which are most spectacular in the spring.

